1.1 THE GHOST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A prior qwen32_85tps_gate.exe was treated as evidence for the 85 TPS ladder.

  ARTIFACT            = F:\~dev\build_p2\Debug\qwen32_85tps_gate.exe
  SHA256              = 2F0DD9329F1ADAE5D52E4A0D575067CC50E908CDCC36476825B66431CFA1086B
  SIZE                = 2890240
  MTIME_UTC           = 2026-09-17T02:26:42.6645239Z
  PDB_PRESENT         = yes (16429056 bytes)
  VCPROJ              = F:\~dev\build_p2\qwen32_85tps_gate.vcxproj (50455 bytes)
  VCPROJ_SOURCE       = F:\~dev\tests\qwen32_85tps_gate.cpp   (a real tracked path)

The .vcxproj was generated by CMake from a target that does not exist in any
tracked file:

  git log -S 'qwen32_85tps_gate' -- CMakeLists.txt   -> NO COMMITS, EVER
  git ls-files build_p2/                              -> UNTRACKED (not in git)
  repo-wide scan of every CMakeLists.txt / *.cmake    -> ZERO definitions

A real artifact, from a real generator input, that no longer exists in any
tracked source. The exe could not be reproduced, could not be tied to a source
identity, and could not be symbolized -- because there was nothing to symbolize
against. Same defect class as the QKV_CPU_FALLBACK ghost.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.2 RESTORATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeLists.txt now defines RAWRXD_DEEP2_CORE_SOURCES, shared by deep2_benchmark
and the new qwen32_85tps_gate, and defines the gate with /Zi /DEBUG:FULL /DEBUG.

Sharing the list is the point: a private 40-entry copy of a source list is how
two targets drift until one of them cannot link. deep2_benchmark previously
listed its own and was missing Deep2B66RuntimeMeta.cpp.


