--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.3 THE FINDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CPU_EXECUTION_FRACTION   = 1280 / 1280 = 1.000
GPU_LAYER_SUBMITS        = 0
STRICT_GPU_VIOLATIONS    = 0
GATE_VERDICT             = PASS
EXIT_CODE                = 0

A run that executed 100% of its 1280 layer-visits on the CPU, with zero GPU
submits of any kind, was certified PASS and exited 0.

The sharpest single statement is the pairing:
  PLANNED_CPU_LAYER_CALLS = 0     the engine intended GPU for all 1280
  GPU_FORWARD_FALLBACKS  = 1280   and achieved GPU for none

This is a DISPATCH failure, not a weight-pipeline failure. The model loaded
(ok=1), the geometry matched, two Vulkan devices initialised, and then every
layer was declined to the host.

It is exactly the condition the wire specification calls
CPU_FALLBACK_VIOLATION (0x10) -- "the silent killer".

ROOT_CAUSE_OF_FALSE_PASS = the gate's only strict check is
  x.size()==ntok && vulkanStrictViolation()==0
and vulkanStrictViolation_ is assigned at whole-forward LANE-SELECTION points
only. It never observes a per-layer fallback. The gate had no instrument
capable of disagreeing with itself.

