PART 3 -- RAWRXD_INFERENCE_WIRE_001
================================================================================

STATUS              = PASS
VERDICT             = PASS  (computed from 58 observations)
CHECKS_TOTAL        = 58
CHECKS_PASS         = 58
CHECKS_FAIL         = 0
EXIT_CODE           = 0

SCOPE               = INSTRUMENT_ONLY_MOVES_NO_BYTES
  Stated in the header and printed by the probe. The wire holds no weights,
  moves no bytes, and makes nothing faster. The residency ledger is a shadow
  mirror fed by caller-reported facts; it is not a cache and evicts nothing.
  Calling it a cache would be the decorative-metric failure this project exists
  to catch.

FRAME_BYTES         = 96 (pack(1), static_assert-enforced)
BATCH_PACKETS       = 1024 frames = 96 KiB per WriteFile

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 THE WIRE SPECIFICATION, AS BUILT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [TOKEN_SEQ][ROUTER_ID][EXPERT_ID][STATE_FLAG][REUSE_DISTANCE][LATENCY_NS]
  plus framing required to make the record checkable:
    magic 'DPTX', version, sizeBytes, gapless packetSeq,
    wallNs + raw QPC (reader needs no time conversion),
    per-frame FNV-1a content hash over the frame with the hash field zeroed.

  0x01 HOT_HIT                0x02 COLD_FAULT          0x04 EMPTY_CONSUMED
  0x08 METAL_BLOCK_THRASH     0x10 CPU_FALLBACK_VIOLATION
  kStateMask = 0x1F, asserted at compile time AND checked at runtime.

  The state byte is unforgeable BY CONSTRUCTION: the emitter refuses any byte
  with a bit outside the mask and COUNTS the rejection. A probe that only tested
  "does 0x01 emit" would not notice a wire accepting 0xFF; this one tests 0x20
  and 0xFF and requires refusal.

  LOCATION AND REPRESENTATION ARE ORTHOGONAL. Tier encodes Absent/Storage/
  FileCache/Host/Gpu and nothing else. Quantized-vs-decoded is not in the enum,
  because folding a representation into a location enum is how a buffer ends up
  reporting a tier it does not hold.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.2 WHAT IS NOW MEASURABLE THAT WAS NOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THRASH_STATE_EMITTABLE   = 1
  CPU_FALLBACK_STATE_EMITTABLE = 1
  TAMPER_DETECTED          = 1
  SEQ_GAP_DETECTED         = 1
  CPU_FALLBACK_VIOLATION_DETECTED_IN_FILE = 8 of 8

  A counter-only design cannot emit METAL_BLOCK_THRASH. A verifier that always
  returns clean verifies nothing. Both are now demonstrably falsifiable.

  reuse_distance is DERIVED, not declared: routing one expert at tokens 1, 4
  and 9 yields 0, 3, 5 (checked REUSE_SECOND_EQ_3 / REUSE_THIRD_EQ_5). A literal
  cannot produce the 2nd and 3rd values from the 1st.

  cold_fraction RESPONDS TO CAPACITY: same 8 experts over two tokens, roomy
  ledger -> frac 0.000 with 8 hits; ledger capped at 16 bytes -> frac > 0 and
  < 1 with some hits. A hardcoded cold_fraction fails one of the two by
  construction.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.3 FOUR DEFECTS THE PROBE CAUGHT BEFORE IT PASSED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The probe did not pass on first run. It failed 6 checks, then 1, then 2, then
passed. All four root causes are recorded because a falsification probe whose
first run is green is not known to work.

DEFECT_1  INSTRUMENT (the worst kind)
  THRASH_REUSE_DISTANCE_KNOWN expected 2, measured 0.
  CAUSE  eviction cleared the slot including lastRoute, destroying the reuse
         distance of exactly the experts whose reuse distance is the whole point.
  FIX    Eviction ring records the victim's lastRoute; reuse distance is
         recovered from the ring when the slot is gone.
  WHY IT MATTERS  reuse_distance < capacity means the eviction policy is broken;
         > capacity means the cache is too small. If eviction erases the number,
         those two diagnoses are indistinguishable and 0x08 is unreachable.

DEFECT_2  MEASUREMENT (worse than the code)
  CF_STARVED_SOME_HITS expected hits>0, measured 0.
  CAUSE  the check routed 8 DISTINCT experts once and expected hits. A first
         touch has no earlier route to hit. The expectation was unsatisfiable by
         construction and the ledger was correct.
  FIX    route the same 8 experts over two tokens; token 2 is where capacity
         discriminates.
  NOTE   This is the project's recurring failure mode: a diagnostic encoding an
         impossible expectation produces a confident wrong conclusion, and the
         instinct is to distrust the system rather than the check.

DEFECT_3  TEST ARITHMETIC
  GAP_REWRITE read 4 frames at offset 3 in a 5-frame file -- only 2 available.
  ReadFile returned short, the comparison failed, applied=0. The resulting
  stream [0][1][3][3][4] produced gaps=2, which is CORRECT and is how the
  arithmetic error was located: the verifier was right and the test was wrong.

DEFECT_4  MISSING SEEK-BACK
  GAP_DETECTED expected gaps=1, measured 0 on a correct-looking 4-frame file.
  CAUSE  ReadFile left the cursor at EOF and the rewrite omitted the seek back to
         the destination slot, so it APPENDED. After truncating, the file held
         the original frames 0..3: contiguous, zero gaps. Diagnosed from the
         measured seq pattern, not by inspection.
  FIX    seek back to the destination offset before writing; truncate to an
         ABSOLUTE length rather than to FILE_END after an in-place overwrite.


================================================================================
PART 4 -- WHAT IS STILL NOT ESTABLISHED
================================================================================

UNRESOLVED
  WHY 1280/1280 layer-visits fell back to the host. The gate records the
       FALLBACK count but not the reason. No dispatch site was instrumented.
       This is now the single highest-value open question: a fallback with a
       known cause is a bug report, a fallback without one is a mystery.

  PDB_GUID / PDB_AGE not extracted. The linker consumed the PDB but the
  CodeView record was not parsed, so the crt-term can be read but is currently
  read=None rather than 1.

  The MLA fast-fail (0xC0000409, RCX=7, int 29h) is UNTOUCHED by this work.
  RVA 0xC3169 and 0xC3134 belonged to deep2_streamer_cert_mla.exe, which does
  not exist in this tree and was not produced by any target in any tracked
  CMakeLists -- the same ghost mechanism as Part 1. Those RVAs are therefore
  NOT symbolizable even with a perfect PDB: the image is gone, and a fresh
  build will not reproduce the offsets.

NOT ATTEMPTED
  No adoption of the wire into tools/deep2_streamer_cert.cpp. The wire builds
  and self-certifies, but no real model run has emitted a packet yet. Until it
  has, every number above describes the INSTRUMENT and not the engine.

  Five 2-byte residency stubs remain 2 bytes and are still referenced by
  rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt: ResidencyTracker, WorkingSetPredictor,
  PredictiveMemoryManager, TensorPlacementManager, CapacityManager.

  rawrxd/certs/mla_cert_001.cpp is 24 bytes ("// Auto-generated stub") and
  rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt:9937 builds it as "MLA-CERT-001 production seal".
  A 108544-byte mla_cert_001.exe exists in build/bin/Release. A named
  production seal that is a stub, with a linked binary, is the exact shape of a
  fabricated certificate.

  rawrxd/CMakeLists.txt defines deep2_streamer_cert TWICE (line 8507 guarded by
  BUILD_DEEP2_STREAMER_CERT, default OFF, and line 18683 unguarded). Enabling
  the option is a configure-time duplicate-target error. Latent, not hit.

  src/deep2/deep2_api.h does not exist. Any saved decision citing it as the
  cert's C API is unsatisfiable against this tree.

